    ################## HYPRLAND BINDINGS NOT MIGRATED ##################

    1. Window / workspace management - excluded by request. Everything in
       default/hypr/bindings/tiling.lua: split, pseudo, float, tiled fullscreen
       (fullscreen inside the window), full width, save/restore width, workspace
       layout toggle, directional focus, scratchpad, move-workspace-to-monitor,
       swap window, resize chords (SUPER +/- minus/equal), mouse binds, window
       grouping, and monitor scaling. Also the window-management overrides in
       hypr/bindings.lua (ALT+Q close, SUPER+K maximize, SUPER+T float,
       SUPER+O pop out, SUPER+D restore to tiling, ALT+TAB switcher) - the
       labwc equivalents are already defined above.

       Since added, because labwc has native actions for them (see the block
       after the resize chords): fullscreen (W-C-f), sticky/pop-out (W-8),
       screen zoom (W-C-z / W-S-C-z / W-C-A-z), monitor focus (C-A-Tab),
       and workspaces 1-4 - jump (W-Tab / W-S-Tab / W-C-Tab, W-A-1..4) and
       move window (W-S-1..4, W-S-A-1..4).

       Still absent because labwc has no such concept: tiling layouts and
       window groups, directional focus (no "focus left" action exists),
       scratchpad, close-all-windows, and per-window transparency or gaps.

    2. Needs hyprctl / Hyprland IPC - excluded by request:
       SUPER+BACKSPACE, SUPER+SHIFT+BACKSPACE     window transparency / gaps toggle
       SUPER+CTRL+BACKSPACE                       single-window square aspect
       SUPER+CTRL+DELETE, +ALT+DELETE             laptop display / mirroring
       SUPER+CTRL+N                               nightlight (hyprctl hyprsunset)
       SUPER+K / SUPER+SHIFT+K                    omarchy-menu-keybindings (reads
                                                  Hyprland's own bind list)
       SUPER+ALT+SHIFT+F                          Files in terminal cwd
                                                  (hyprctl activewindow)
       SUPER+ALT+[ / ]                            webcam overlay resize
       SUPER+C / SUPER+V / SUPER+X                universal copy/paste/cut - these
                                                  inject keys with Hyprland's
                                                  sendkeystate dispatcher; labwc
                                                  has no equivalent action
       switch:on/off:Lid Switch                   lid handling; not a keybind, and
                                                  labwc has no switch bindings
       RETURN/TAB/arrows inside a slurp selection Hyprland binds these only while
                                                  the selection layer is open

    3. Key already taken by a live binding in this file - NOT migrated, listed
       here so the choice is visible:
       SUPER+SPACE           Omarchy menu        (W-space types the primary selection)
       SUPER+SHIFT+SPACE     Toggle top bar      (S-W-space opens the root menu)
       SUPER+RETURN          Terminal            (W-Return raises the @Work terminal)
       SUPER+SHIFT+B         Browser             (W-S-b is the BANNER terminal;
